      <item>
        <title>WRO Costa Rica 2017 - Latakia 2030</title>
        <description>&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-is-wro&quot;&gt;What is WRO?&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The World Robot Olympiad is a global robotics competition for young people, built around Lego Mindstorms from LEGO Education. It started in Singapore in 2004 and now draws more than 26,000 teams from over 65 countries.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Open Category is project-based. Teams build their own robotics solution around the theme of the season and present it to a group of judges on competition day.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;latakia-2030&quot;&gt;Latakia 2030&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Latakia 2030 is our picture of what Syria could be by 2030: a country that runs on current technology — green building, clean energy, data mining, image processing, virtual and augmented reality, machine learning and computer vision.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We chose Latakia as the place to start because of its history and its geography. It has the sea, the mountains and a living city, all in one place.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;iframe width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;315&quot; src=&quot;https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/p3rBSB9RmV4&quot; title=&quot;YouTube video player&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allow=&quot;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture&quot; allowfullscreen=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;

